{
  "capture": {
    "commit": "e7d164b3eb58d09dcaebee02374e91eb71a51bdc",
    "decision": "DECISIONS #39: public record minus id, exact derivative bytes, meta.json minus id/createdAt",
    "placeholders": {
      "@@ID@@": "the generated material id; it occurs once in each derivative and in the stored file names",
      "@@ID@@:<name>": "the generated id of the record made for the sample of that name (duplicateOf)",
      "@@STORE_ROOT_SHA256@@": "meta.storeId, the sha256 of the absolute store directory",
      "@@DERIVATIVE_SHA256@@": "meta.derivativeSha256, the sha256 of the derivative bytes with the id filled in"
    },
    "method": "The unmodified e7d164b ingestAttachment ran on the four round-1 legacy samples (the validator generator's legacy set), each alone in a fresh store; attachmentPublic gave the public record, the store files gave the derivative bytes and meta.json. A second set of fresh stores gave identical normalized results. Round 1 answered a second upload of the same bytes (legacy-as.docx after legacy.doc) with a duplicateOf record of the first; later builds re-evaluate refused bytes instead (reusableDerivative), so every upload below is recorded on its own and the duplicate answer is not part of the golden.",
    "ownerless": "The single-user local port drops meta.ownerId; normalizeUpload removes an ownerId key if a store still writes one, so the golden compares the ownerless shape."
  },
